      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While air in the pipes can cause noise, the rhythmic, physical knocking sound doesn't typically point to an air pocket issue. Typically, issues like this in water heaters are mechanical, related to moving parts or corrosion. However, it's not always a hardware failure – sometimes, the heating element itself can cause vibrations. A plumber with experience with water heaters can help you pinpoint the source of the noise and provide a more specific diagnosis.",
